# demo-video transcript template — the Claude turn claude-hero.cast's second pass appends (Issue #2381)
#
# One Claude Code session turn in the JSONL dialect
# src/lib/hooks/sources/claude/transcript.ts reads, shaped like
# claude-delegate.jsonl: the operator's prompt (`origin.kind: human`,
# `promptSource: typed` — the markers #2196 requires before a `user` row is
# written), an assistant record that calls Bash with `npm run test:unit`, its
# `tool_result`, and the closing assistant record (`stop_reason: end_turn` with
# prose — what #2264 requires before the turn may be written).
#
# The prompt is `{{TASK}}`, not `{{MESSAGE}}`: by the time this row plays the
# last submission is the approval answer ("1"), and `{{TASK}}` is the first line
# of the pass's first submission — the instruction the phone approved. The
# scene that sends it keeps it to one line for exactly this reason. The
# tool_result is a literal: there is no `@exec` on this pass, so `{{EXEC_OUTPUT}}`
# would still be the delegation's `ask` output.
#
# The last record's text is the Markdown the chat surface renders; the
# `[Header.tsx](src/components/layout/Header.tsx)` link is what becomes a
# ChatFileLink (#2345), and the phone taps it. No personal path: `cwd` is the
# seed worktree.
